-No blur implementation is added to st itself. Scrollback/reflow is not ready.
+No blur implementation is added to st itself. Scrollback holds 2000 physical
+rows, with resize reflow of the default screen/history and separate alternate
+screen contents. Shift+PageUp/PageDown scrolls a page; the wheel scrolls three
+rows unless the application requests mouse events (Shift overrides it).
+Column changes clear the selection. The core is tested with ASan/UBSan and
+synthetic input, not a live terminal session.
+
+History/reflow adapts the suckless community scrollback 0.9.2 and reflow 0.9.2
+patches, based on work by BeyondMagic et al. The bounded resize ring and wide
+cell handling follow bakkeby/st-flexipatch (MIT/X Consortium license). Sources
+and provenance are retained in the parent wm repository under patches/upstream.
 Color emoji and visual rendering still need a later authorized visual test.
 TERM remains st-256color; prepare matching terminfo during future installation,
 including remote hosts where it is needed. Do not substitute TERM blindly.
